    "title": "Detroit Pistons guard Cade Cunningham hurt lung: Here's what it means",
    "text": "PISTONSCade Cunningham has collapsed lung; a doc explains what that means Omari Sankofa IIDetroit Free PressUpdated March 19, 2026, 7:50 p.m. ETSubscribe to hear this storyWASHINGTON – The Detroit Pistons will be without their superstar for at least two weeks.Guard Cade Cunningham has suffered a left lung pneumothorax, more commonly known as a lung collapse. He exited the first quarter against the Washington Wizards on Tuesday, March 17, after a collision with rookie wing Tre Johnson and didn't return. The team announced a two-week re-evaluation timeline on Thursday.",
